# OWNERS — Pipelines as Code (PaC) authorization
#
# PaC (running in the cluster's pipelines namespace) reads this Prow-style file
# from the DEFAULT branch to decide who may trigger a PipelineRun on a
# pull_request without a maintainer commenting `/ok-to-test`.
#
# Why this repo needs one: PaC's Forgejo ACL recognises repo COLLABORATORS,
# this file, or an `/ok-to-test` comment. Org membership does not count, so
# without this file every pull_request event from a non-collaborator is
# refused with "User <name> is not allowed to trigger CI via pull_request in
# this repo" — even for an org owner.
#
# In PaC, `approvers` and `reviewers` have EQUAL power to trigger CI; only the
# `.*` (root) scope is honored.
#
# b4mad-release-agent is listed below because enabling it is the whole point
# of this skill: its release commit and tag push to main is itself a
# CI-triggering event, and the GitHub-bot auto-exemption this pattern usually
# relies on does not apply on Forgejo/Codeberg.
#
# ⚠️ This skill does NOT guess your human approvers/reviewers — a git remote's
# owner segment is an org or a fork target, not necessarily a person with
# review authority, and inventing a name here would be worse than an empty
# list. Add yourself and your other maintainers below before relying on this
# file to authorise your own pull requests.
#
# Docs: https://pipelinesascode.com/docs/guide/running/

approvers:
  - b4mad-release-agent
  # - <your-forgejo-username>
  # - <a-second-approver>
